# Study Hub — Cursor Rules
# Electron + React desktop app: connect Blackboard once, Today tells you what matters.
# Read this file and docs/PROJECT_BRIEF.md before every response.

## IDENTITY
"Connect Blackboard once. Every day Study Hub tells you what matters and
gets you ready for it." The Blackboard mirror (files, announcements,
assignments, the student's own grades) is the engine; Today is the product:
a ranked daily plan (assignments, exam prep, grade risk, needed score) with
one action per item. Built-in study tools get the student ready: notes,
glossary, exam-aware SM-2 flashcards, practice tests, grade calculator, and
Nova, the 3D companion who runs review sessions.
An optional cloud "Commons" (shared study materials, grade distributions,
professor reviews) is deferred until alpha usage justifies it.
It is a native desktop window via Electron, NOT a web app.

## ARCHITECTURE: LOCAL-FIRST + OPTIONAL COMMONS
- Personal data (courses, notes, cards, mastery, own grades, BB mirror)
  lives ONLY in local SQLite. Works offline, no account.
- Commons (Supabase) is opt-in, requires a verified .edu account, and only
  receives items the student explicitly publishes.
- Every feature must work without Commons and without an API key.

## TECH STACK
- Runtime: Electron (main) + React 18 (renderer), Vite
- Styling: Bootstrap reset ONLY + custom --sh-* CSS tokens
- Notes editor: TipTap
- Database: better-sqlite3 via IPC (db:* handlers)
- File parsing: officeparser v6 (PPTX/DOCX/XLSX), pdf-parse (PDF), main only
- AI: Claude Haiku via main-process IPC (optional)
- Cloud: Supabase (Commons only, Phase 4+)

## FILE STRUCTURE
electron/
 main.cjs              Main process, file/AI IPC
 preload.cjs           Renderer bridge (window.studyHub)
 database.cjs          SQLite init, schema, numbered migrations
 dbHandlers.cjs        All db:* IPC handlers
 blackboardWindow.cjs  Embedded Blackboard window + mirror sync
 bbPreload.cjs         Blackboard window bridge
 aiConfig.cjs          API key (safeStorage)
 anthropicClient.cjs   Claude calls
 maintenance.cjs       Daily backups (keep 7), restore, app info, updater

src/
 app/StudyHubApp.jsx   Root app, course state, routing, first-run setup gate
 features/             Feature modules (today, decks, grades, settings, setup,
                       dashboard/calendar, import, practice, web, commons UI)
 features/today/       Priority engine (pure, unit-tested) + Home/Today screens
 hub/                  HubScreen (hub views) + user course view (UserCourseApp)
 study/                OM 300 built-in course, FlashcardDeck, sm2.js
 session/              Session shell, shield meter, results, rounds, power-ups
 companion/            Nova 3D companion, quiz panel, tours, XP, voice packs
 pptx/ ai/ syllabus/   Import pipelines
 db/courseStore.js     Data access layer (renderer's only DB entry point)
 commons/              Commons client
 shell/                Rail, title bar, command palette, ShellContext,
                       motion.js, pack.js, ambient background
 studyhub-bootstrap.css  ONLY CSS file

supabase/              Commons SQL schema, RLS, edge functions
docs/                  PROJECT_BRIEF.md, ROADMAP.md, PRODUCT_BACKLOG.md

## CSS DESIGN SYSTEM
Hard-edged HUD on true black. Spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-01-ui-overhaul-design.md.
NEVER hardcode colors, fonts, radii or shadows. ALWAYS use tokens
(defined in :root of studyhub-bootstrap.css; color-mix() over tokens is fine):
 Surfaces: --sh-bg --sh-side --sh-panel --sh-panel-strong --sh-panel-solid (floating UI)
 Lines: --sh-border --sh-border-strong --sh-track
 Accent: --sh-accent --sh-accent-soft --sh-accent-line --sh-accent-hover
 Secondary: --sh-accent-2 (magenta) ONLY for chamfer/card corner marks, ambient
  lines, auras, exam tags/edges, the mastery/progress gradient end, formula rule
 States: --sh-warn(-soft/-line) --sh-danger(-soft/-line)
 Power-ups: --sh-power (green) only on power-up drops
 Text: --sh-text --sh-text-2 --sh-text-3 (never dimmer than text-3)
 Shape: radius is 0 everywhere; --sh-cut chamfer; --sh-shadow-panel --sh-glow-accent
--sh-accent (aqua in Nova, red in Zombies) is the only interactive accent. No terminal green.
Glow only on the single most important element on screen.

Typography (fonts bundled via @fontsource, never a CDN):
 - Display: --sh-font-display (Michroma), uppercase, letter-spacing 0.06em
 - Content: --sh-font-body (Geist). Task titles 17-18px / 600.
 - Numbers, times, codes, HUD labels: --sh-font-mono (Geist Mono)
 - Scale: 11 / 12.5 / 14 / 17-18 / 22-24 / 28-30. Minimum 11px.

Motion: respect html[data-motion="reduced"] (set from Settings or the OS via
src/shell/motion.js). Never use @media (prefers-reduced-motion) directly.

Tab active state: border-bottom only (2px solid var(--sh-accent)); vertical nav:
2px left border. Never a full border.

Flavor packs ("Make it yours"): src/shell/pack.js sets html[data-pack]
("nova" default | "zombies"), stored in localStorage studyHub.v2.prefs.pack.
A pack overrides TOKEN VALUES only (html[data-pack="zombies"] block after :root),
plus art layers, Nova's shader look, voice lines (src/companion/packs/) and
celebrations (medals vs power-ups). Layout never changes between packs. Never
write per-component pack colors; anything reading tokens in JS (ambient canvas,
Nova shader) must refresh on the studyhub-pack-changed event.

## IPC PATTERN
Main: ipcMain.handle('namespace:action', async (_, args) => {})
Preload exposes via window.studyHub. Renderer calls the bridge only.
NEVER require() Node modules in renderer. NEVER use remote module.

## DATABASE RULES
- All course data in SQLite. localStorage only for UI prefs, OM 300
  built-in progress, and the migration flag.
- Renderer uses courseStore.js, not raw IPC.
- Writes are UPSERTS KEYED BY uuid. NEVER delete-and-reinsert a whole
  course/deck/component list (it cascades and destroys mastery + grades).
- Transactions for multi-table writes. Foreign keys ON. WAL ON.
- Schema changes go in a new numbered migration in database.cjs.

## SECURITY RULES
- API key only in main process, encrypted with safeStorage. Never in
  renderer, never in localStorage.
- File open/read IPC only for paths in the allowlist; the allowlist is
  populated by native dialogs, imports, and the BB temp dir — never by
  arbitrary renderer input.
- Blackboard bridge only honored on *.blackboard.com origins.
- Escape any user/slide text injected into Blackboard pages.

## GUARDRAILS (COMMONS + BLACKBOARD)
- Commons accepts only student-authored content. Block raw professor
  files, exams, quizzes, answer keys by default. Everything reportable.
- Web study guides stored as link + summary/cards, never re-hosted.
- Grade distributions: anonymous, self-reported, shown only at >= 5 reports.
- Professor reviews: structured ratings + <=280 chars, filtered, 1 per
  student per course-term.
- Blackboard: read-only, logged-in student's own data, human pace,
  no stored credentials.

## COMPONENT RULES
UserCourseApp module tabs: CONTENT | NOTES | GLOSSARY | GRADES
 plus QZ-01 as a DRILL sidebar item.
Active sidebar state: 'module:{uuid}' | 'qz-deck' | null. Never array index.
Definition list: high confidence plain, medium = amber square marker,
 low = NEEDS REVIEW section.
Section blocks: numbered (01 02 in mono aqua), bullets (— prefix),
 deflist (term above, definition indented).
Show 4 items by default, expand for more. Collapsible threshold: 120 chars.
Hub views (hubView): today | plan | calendar | decks | grades | settings | courses.
 Settings tabs: general | nova | theme | blackboard | backup | ai.
Sessions (quiz + flashcards) render inside SessionShell (sets html[data-session],
 collapses the rail, Nova moves to the session lane). Nothing may open a second
 session while one is open. Ratings Again/Hard/Good/Easy = keys 1-4 = SM-2 grades
 1/3/4/5. Shield: misses hit shields first; health drops only while shields are down.
Rounds: 5 marks per round in SQLite settings key session.rounds (recordMark);
 completed sessions and newly completed assignments add a mark.

## KEYBOARD HANDLERS
Flashcard drill: check palette closed, useCallback, cleanup in effect,
 200ms flip debounce via ref, ignore keys while a rating is in flight.
Chapter arrow keys: stop when activeItem === 'qz-deck' and when focus is
 in an input, textarea, or contentEditable.

## AI ENHANCEMENT
Model: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 for enhancement (never Sonnet/Opus).
Graceful fallback: no key, API failure, invalid JSON.
Local pipeline runs first; AI enhances, never replaces. Flag enhancedByAI.

## WHAT NEVER TO TOUCH
- OM 300 built-in course content (src/study/sections, src/glossary/courseData.js)
- officeparser/pdf-parse in the renderer bundle (keep in Vite externals)
- Bootstrap classes for layout logic

## BUILD REQUIREMENTS
Every code change must:
1. Pass npm run build
2. Keep officeparser out of the renderer bundle
3. Add no console.log / console.error in production paths
4. Not break the OM 300 course

## AGENT WORKFLOW (subagents)
Delegate to subagents by default whenever it helps; don't wait to be asked.
- Plans with independent tasks: execute with superpowers subagent-driven-development
 (one implementer subagent per task, then a review subagent).
- Broad codebase searches / "how does X work": explore subagent.
- 2+ independent investigations or edits on disjoint files: run subagents in parallel.
- Keep in the main agent: user questions, design approval, final verification
 (build + vitest) and commits.

## COMMIT MESSAGE FORMAT
"Phase X.Y — Short description

- Bullet 1
- Bullet 2"

